During 2001–2025, cold-stress changes became more mixed, with increases across portions of the northern and central interior and decreases in scattered eastern areas (@fig-oab-cold-stress-recent). Heat stress continued to increase primarily in the Southwest and southern Great Plains (@fig-oab-heat-stress-recent). Significant suitability increases were more limited but remained evident in portions of the northern United States (@fig-oab-suitability-recent).


